                "Using WHERE and HAVING correctly is essential for writing accurate SQL queries, especially when aggregate functions and GROUP BY are involved.",
            example:
                "WHERE can filter employees whose salary is above ₹50,000 before grouping. HAVING can then filter departments whose resulting employee count is greater than five.",
