            topicId: null,
            duration: "15 min",
            difficulty: "Advanced",
            completed: false,
            locked: false,
            type: "lesson",
            description:
                "Learn how JOINs can be combined with window functions to perform advanced analytical calculations.",
            definition:
                "Window functions calculate values across related rows without collapsing them into a single row per group. When combined with JOINs, they can provide analytical calculations across data from multiple tables.",
            whyItMatters:
                "This combination is powerful for ranking, running totals, comparisons, and advanced business analysis.",
